{%- comment -%}
  fye-wishlist-button — the heart.

  Rewired 01/09/2026. Two contexts, because a heart means two different things
  depending on where it is pressed:

    context: 'form'   the product page. The shopper may have chosen a metal, a
                      quality, a centre stone, a side pair and an engraving,
                      and NONE of that exists in Liquid — it lives in the buy
                      box, in the DOM, at the moment of the click. So the
                      button carries no payload; fye-ui.js reads the form.

    context: 'card'   a grid tile, a related row, a search result. Nothing is
                      configured, so the payload IS the product: handle,
                      default variant, title, image. Static, known at render.

  Ed, 01/09/2026: the heart saves THE WHOLE CONFIGURATION, and the wishlist
  card shows the configured price. That is the whole reason for the split
  above — live saves a bare product id, so a shopper who spent ten minutes
  configuring a trilogy gets back an unconfigured product page.

  ── PRICE IS NEVER SAVED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Only what identifies the ring is stored. Money and availability are read
  LIVE when the wishlist renders. A ring saved in March and opened in
  September must not quote March's price — metal moves, and a stale figure in
  a list shared with a partner is a promise we did not make.

  Parameters:
    product   required
    variant   optional; defaults to the product's selected-or-first
    context   'form' | 'card'   (default 'card')
    label     optional visible text; icon-only when blank
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ctx = context | default: 'card'
  assign v = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign img = product.featured_image | default: v.image
-%}

<button type="button"
        class="wish{% if label == blank %} wish--icon{% else %} wish--labelled{% endif %}{% if size == 'lg' %} wish--lg{% endif %}"
        data-fye-wish="{{ ctx }}"
        aria-pressed="false"
        {%- if ctx == 'card' %}
          data-wish-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
          data-wish-variant="{{ v.id }}"
          data-wish-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
          data-wish-image="{{ img | image_url: width: 300 }}"
        {%- endif %}
        aria-label="{{ label | default: 'Save' }} {{ product.title | escape }}">
  {%- render 'icon', name: 'heart', class: 'icon--sm' -%}
  {%- if label != blank -%}
    <span class="wish__label">{{ label }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
</button>
